# Barrel imports

When a directory has an `index.ts` barrel, import from the parent alias — not from subfolders or individual files.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — bypasses the barrel
import { RequireAuth } from '@/features/auth';
import type { TAttendeesFormValues } from '@/features/types';
import { useAuth } from '@/hooks/useAuth';
import { AuthContext } from '@context/auth/AuthContext';

// ❌ BAD — same barrel, split across lines
import { RequireAuth } from '@/features';
import { RegistrationForm, RegistrationHeroSection } from '@/features';

// ✅ GOOD — one import per barrel path
import { RequireAuth, RegistrationForm, RegistrationHeroSection } from '@/features';
import { useAuth, useAuthForm } from '@/hooks';
import { AuthContext } from '@/context';
```

Combine value and type imports from the same barrel in one statement:

```typescript
import { RequireAuth, type TAttendeesFormValues } from '@/features';
```

## Rules

1. **Export new public APIs** from the nearest `index.ts` (`features`, `hooks`, `context`, `pages`, `services`, etc.).
2. **Consumers import from the barrel** (`@/features`, `@/hooks`, `@/context`) unless importing from within the same feature folder (relative imports are fine).
3. **One import statement per barrel path** — never duplicate `from '@/features'` (or any other barrel) on separate lines.
4. **Do not add new top-level dirs** like `components/` when an existing module fits (`features/auth/`, `shared/`, `ui/`).
